PURPOSE of /kernel/wireless_tests/utility/ping4
Decription: Ping (IPv4) test using established connections
Author: Ken Benoit <kbenoit@redhat.com>

0.Purpose
=========
This is meant to perform a ping test. This can be performed in a couple of
different ways. In a multihost setup where there are SERVERS and CLIENTS defined
each client will request all the IPv4 addresses on each server and then ping all
of those addresses one at a time, verifying a minimum amount of packets are
received back after transmission. In a STANDALONE setup then a default value
of "beaker.engineering.redhat.com" is used (if PING_TARGET is not defined) and
that target (or targets) will be pinged making sure that the minimum amount of
packets are received back after transmission.

1.Files
=======
Makefile - used to run the test script.
runtest.sh - script that performs the setup and install process of the custom
             kernel.
PURPOSE - this file.

2.Process
=========
Simply run the following command:
# make run

3.Test params
=============
This /kernel/wireless_tests/utility/ping4 test accepts the following parameters
passed in from Beaker.

$PING_TARGET - a space separated list of IPv4 addresses or hostnames to ping
               (optional).

-end PURPOSE file
